            {
                "entry_id": "ce639188-3294-367e-bf01-99865697ec20",
                "word": "lallation",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "aff637b8-7422-4d6c-bbec-14f267ca58e0",
                        "entry_id": "ce639188-3294-367e-bf01-99865697ec20",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "lallations"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bdc2b5ea-5a53-3360-89e0-a80c23827a01",
                        "entry_id": "ce639188-3294-367e-bf01-99865697ec20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Défaut de prononciation qui consiste à appuyer sur les \\\"l\\\" mal à propos, comme si chacune de ces lettres était double, ou à les mouiller indûment, ou à les substituer à la lettre r."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6a7c5dc0-7d09-3420-8565-55f7ff6119e3",
                        "entry_id": "ce639188-3294-367e-bf01-99865697ec20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Émissions vocales prélinguistiques du bébé à partir de 5 mois, émissions qui font apparaître une gamme d’expressions sonores plus étendue que celle utilisée par la langue de l’environnement."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b7d4261-0ac3-4ecd-abdf-1928622050a0",
                                "sense_id": "6a7c5dc0-7d09-3420-8565-55f7ff6119e3",
                                "text": "Jusqu’à environ 3 mois, vous aurez le plaisir d’entendre votre enfant s’adonner à la lallation (aux gazouillis). Cette étape permet au nourrisson de s’essayer aux premières voyelles. Le \"a\" apparaît tout d’abord, et les parents découvrent bientôt les célèbres \"aheu\" (bébé ne sait pas encore prononcer les \"r\" !). La lallation, ou plus communément appelée le jasis, est moins un moyen de communication qu’un plaisir vocal de l'enfant."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9065cb4a-ada7-4775-987e-15e4b048bdd2",
                        "source_entry_id": "ce639188-3294-367e-bf01-99865697ec20",
                        "source_sense_description": "défaut de prononciation",
                        "target_lang_word": "lallation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lallation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e034e6dd-410d-3611-9dce-759dadf94e4e",
                                        "entry_id": "b7ec732b-5042-3d8c-8f7e-dde62bdf8555",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The incorrect pronunciation of the letter \\\"r\\\" so that it sounds like an \\\"l\\\" (or \\\"w\\\")."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad7bb0e8-a7a2-4aa1-8f74-d36cf2ee6325",
                                                "sense_id": "e034e6dd-410d-3611-9dce-759dadf94e4e",
                                                "text": "She spoke Aramaic with a lazy lallation, affected by many because it was the natural speech of a class."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31b1058a-86cc-4a00-b6ba-047dec4714e0",
                                                "sense_id": "e034e6dd-410d-3611-9dce-759dadf94e4e",
                                                "text": "“Everybody wovs you,” Mary Madelyn said to Melchior.\nWhenever she pronounced an el it became doubleu. […] Except for her partial lallation she spoke well […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2cd5a8bd-81c4-3b37-97d9-b0c0ee5c33a2",
                                        "entry_id": "b7ec732b-5042-3d8c-8f7e-dde62bdf8555",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Baby-talk or gibberish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ffe2e2f-c8c9-4d2f-b0af-62bdf01c7f6d",
                                                "sense_id": "2cd5a8bd-81c4-3b37-97d9-b0c0ee5c33a2",
                                                "text": "1648, Robert Baron, Erotopaignion, Or the Cyprian Academy, London: J. Hardesty et al., “To the Ladies and Gentlewoemen of England,”\nWhen you talke with your children you expect from them no congruence or quaint language, yet you are often pleased to heare them prattle, & are delighted with their lisping Ideoms. This makes me hope that you will dispence with the Lallation & Low dialect of this babe, whose tone is rude, yet his meaning is plaine dealing, which according to the proverbe is a jewell, and consequently most fit for Ladies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04ad447f-0281-4c98-be50-2fdf5a805f86",
                                                "sense_id": "2cd5a8bd-81c4-3b37-97d9-b0c0ee5c33a2",
                                                "text": "The auto-imitation in lallation, a form of spontaneous talking, precedes the imitation of strange words and sounds. […] in lallation the infant follows his own inclination, while in imitating the sound heard from others he will have to accommodate himself to a strange perception."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bbd9be4-d2c3-4441-9617-9eb336c68462",
                                                "sense_id": "2cd5a8bd-81c4-3b37-97d9-b0c0ee5c33a2",
                                                "text": "The chronic effects of the barbiturates on neurological and psychic function resemble those of alcohol. There may be dizziness, clumsiness and ataxia; dysarthria, nystagmus, mental disturbances, nervousness, tremor, lallation, confusion, peculiar behavior, weakness of judgment, emotional instability and hallucinations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
